# Build output. Copying these in would ship a Windows-built bin/ into a linux image and, worse, make the
# layer cache miss on every local build.
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Runtime state that must never be baked into an image: a database carrying somebody's library, the logs
# that describe it, and the generated previews.
**/logs/
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-shm
**/*.sqlite-wal
**/thumbnails/
**/backup/
**/ffmpeg/

# The deployment's own configuration, which names real folders on a real NAS. The image DOES ship the
# repository's own src/DlnaServer.Host/config.json, baked in explicitly (Dockerfile:27,79) - what this
# excludes is a root-level config.json a developer might keep for local testing, plus the saved-off
# copies the admin UI leaves behind.
config.json
**/config.json.saved-*

# Secrets for the admin-remote compose stack - an admin password hash and whatever else operators put
# there. COPY . . (Dockerfile:40) would otherwise put it straight into the build context and image layers.
# Every .env* is excluded, then .env.example is re-included below - later lines win, so order matters.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# Tooling and editor state. graphify-out/ and .claude/ arrived at the context root when the
# Current/ folder was flattened away; the graph alone is tens of megabytes of generated JSON.
.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vs/
.claude/
graphify-out/

# Local media used for manual testing - never part of an image.
media/
**/*.user
**/.DS_Store

# Documentation - large, and changing a markdown file should not invalidate the restore layer.
*.md
docs/
tools/
NasBuild.sh
NasBuild.usage.txt

# Except the release notes, which the Host copies into its output as an operator-facing file: excluded,
# the container build fails at publish with MSB3030 while a local build succeeds. It arrives in the
# `COPY . .` layer, after the restore layer, so the reason for the rule above still holds.
!release-notes.md

# Docker's own files.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
